<article class="env-example" id="03B7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03B7">Example <span data-tag="03B7">10.161.9</span>.</a> Lemma <a href="/tag/032L" data-tag="032L">10.161.8</a> does not work if the ring is not Noetherian. For example consider the action of $G = \{ +1, -1\} $ on $A = \mathbf{C}[x_1, x_2, x_3, \ldots ]$ where $-1$ acts by mapping $x_ i$ to $-x_ i$. The invariant ring $R = A^ G$ is the $\mathbf{C}$-algebra generated by all $x_ ix_ j$. Hence $R \subset A$ is not finite. But $R$ is a normal domain with fraction field $K = L^ G$ the $G$-invariants in the fraction field $L$ of $A$. And clearly $A$ is the integral closure of $R$ in $L$. </p>
</article>